such that later if I want to open it up again,
这样以后如果我想再次打开它，

00:22:22.140 --> 00:22:26.090
I can click Load from your computer and load that file that I've just saved.
我可以点击“从电脑加载”，加载我刚刚保存的那个文件。

00:22:26.090 --> 00:22:28.550
But also, if you create a Scratch account
而且，如果你创建一个Scratch账号

00:22:28.550 --> 00:22:31.850
by clicking on this Join Scratch button, if you don't already have it, and then
如果你还没有账号，点击“加入Scratch”按钮，然后

00:22:31.850 --> 00:22:34.010
sign into your account, you'll have the ability
登录你的账号，你就有能力

00:22:34.010 --> 00:22:36.290
to save projects to Scratch's own website.
把项目保存到Scratch自己的网站上。

00:22:36.290 --> 00:22:38.090
And once you do that if you'd like to, you
一旦你这么做了，如果你愿意，你

00:22:38.090 --> 00:22:41.570
could share your project with the world, to send it to friends and family,
可以把你的项目分享到全世界，发给朋友和家人，

00:22:41.570 --> 00:22:44.780
and to let other people that are using Scratch have an opportunity to see
让其他使用Scratch的人也有机会看到

00:22:44.780 --> 00:22:48.270
your project and try it out as well.
你的项目并试用一下。

00:22:48.270 --> 00:22:51.920
So now that we have the ability to create these sprites
既然我们现在有能力创建这些角色了

00:22:51.920 --> 00:22:55.100
and put them onto the stage, we can create whatever environment
并把它们放到舞台上，我们就能创建任何环境

00:22:55.100 --> 00:22:58.280
we want for the story, or for the animation, or for the game,
无论是为故事、动画、游戏

00:22:58.280 --> 00:23:02.120
or for the other program, that we might be trying to create in Scratch.
还是为我们可能想用Scratch创建的其他程序。

00:23:02.120 --> 00:23:05.120
But right now these sprites aren't really doing anything.
但目前这些角色并没有真正做什么。

00:23:05.120 --> 00:23:06.930
The stage is always staying the same.
舞台始终保持不变。

00:23:06.930 --> 00:23:08.600
The fish are always the same.
鱼也始终不变。

00:23:08.600 --> 00:23:10.670
And, ultimately, what we're going to look at next
接下来，我们要探讨的

00:23:10.670 --> 00:23:13.760
is about programming, how it is that we can write code.
是编程，也就是我们如何编写代码。

00:23:13.760 --> 00:23:17.210
And in particular, by using these blocks and assembling them together
具体来说，就是通过使用这些积木并把它们组合起来

00:23:17.210 --> 00:23:21.260
into stacks of blocks that perform various different activities and tasks,
形成能执行各种不同活动和任务的积木堆，

00:23:21.260 --> 00:23:24.830
we're going to be programming these sprites in the backdrop and the stage,
我们将对背景和舞台中的这些角色进行编程

00:23:24.830 --> 00:23:27.140
to do what we want them to do, to create all the more
让它们按照我们的意愿行事，从而创造出更多

00:23:27.140 --> 00:23:30.140
interactive stories and games and animations
互动式故事、游戏和动画

00:23:30.140 --> 00:23:33.080
that we can create all through the use of Scratch.
这些都可以通过使用Scratch来实现。

00:23:33.080 --> 00:23:34.650
But we'll explore that next time.
不过我们下次再深入探讨。

00:23:34.650 --> 00:23:36.780
That's it for an introduction to Scratch for today.
今天关于Scratch的介绍就到这里。

00:23:36.780 --> 00:23:39.500
And next time, we'll take a look at how we can take that stage
下次，我们将看看如何利用那个舞台

00:23:39.500 --> 00:23:42.610
and begin programming with it as well.
并开始用它进行编程。
